This Express app uses node-auth0 for a browser-based redirect login, stores the session across requests, and refreshes tokens on expiry. Decide which SDK to migrate to and rewrite the session handling.

```ts
import { AuthenticationClient } from 'auth0';
const auth = new AuthenticationClient({ domain, clientId, clientSecret });
app.get('/login', (req, res) => {
  const authUrl = `https://${domain}/authorize?client_id=${clientId}&redirect_uri=${redirectUri}&response_type=code&scope=openid profile email offline_access`;
  res.redirect(authUrl);
});
app.get('/callback', async (req, res) => {
  const resp = await auth.oauth.authorizationCodeGrant({ code: req.query.code, redirect_uri: redirectUri });
  req.session.tokens = { accessToken: resp.data.access_token, refreshToken: resp.data.refresh_token, expiresAt: Date.now() + resp.data.expires_in * 1000 };
  res.redirect('/');
});
app.get('/api/data', async (req, res) => {
  if (Date.now() > req.session.tokens.expiresAt) {
    const resp = await auth.oauth.refreshTokenGrant({ refresh_token: req.session.tokens.refreshToken });
    req.session.tokens.accessToken = resp.data.access_token;
    req.session.tokens.expiresAt = Date.now() + resp.data.expires_in * 1000;
  }
  res.json({ data: 'protected' });
});
```

Migrate this Express callback handler to @auth0/auth0-server-js. The app wants the SDK to own the session.

```ts
import { AuthenticationClient } from 'auth0';
const auth = new AuthenticationClient({ domain, clientId, clientSecret });
app.get('/callback', async (req, res) => {
  const resp = await auth.oauth.authorizationCodeGrant({ code: req.query.code, redirect_uri: redirectUri });
  const expiresAtMs = Date.now() + resp.data.expires_in * 1000;
  req.session.user = { sub: resp.data.id_token_claims.sub, accessToken: resp.data.access_token, expiresAtMs };
  res.redirect('/');
});
```
